# SysGeterrnomsg answers the platform's text for every number but 0, never
# the null string (`r[rxunixsys.index.errno]`); the oracle answers from a table of its own, and
# `Unknown` for a number outside it. The texts of the numbers below are those
# every platform words alike; `{ENAME}` is the host's number for the error.
ruled
say SysGeterrnomsg(0)
say SysGeterrnomsg({EPERM}) '|' SysGeterrnomsg({ENOENT}) '|' SysGeterrnomsg({EACCES}) '|' SysGeterrnomsg({EEXIST})
say SysGeterrnomsg({ENOTDIR}) '|' SysGeterrnomsg({EISDIR}) '|' SysGeterrnomsg({EINVAL}) '|' SysGeterrnomsg({ENOTEMPTY})
empty = ''
do n = -1 to 140
  if SysGeterrnomsg(n) == '' then empty = empty n
end
if SysGeterrnomsg(2147483647) == '' then empty = empty 2147483647
say 'null strings:'||empty
